// Card names that are plural. A proper name has the number of what it names: most are singular,
// and some are plural, naming a collection (*the Hebrides*, *the Beatles*; CGEL, Ch. 5 §20.1,
// p. 515; §20.2.1, p. 517). The number is the name's, not its form's: *Mizzium Mortars deals 4
// damage*, *When King Solomon's Frogs enters* and *Borborygmos and Fblthp enters* are singular,
// so every name not listed here is. Each name here takes plural agreement in its own Oracle text,
// under its full or its Shortened Name [CR#201.5c] (*When The Notary Hobbits enter*, *Whenever
// Bebop & Rocksteady attack or block*).
[
    "Aang and Katara",
    "Aang and La, Ocean's Fury",
    "Bebop & Rocksteady",
    "Casey & Raph, Hotheads",
    "Cloak and Dagger, Entwined",
    "Dark Leo & Shredder",
    "Don & Raph, Hard Science",
    "Donnie & April, Adorkable Duo",
    "Falcon and Redwing",
    "Gert and Old Lace, Runaways",
    "Krang & Shredder",
    "Lo and Li, Twin Tutors",
    "Mikey & Mona, Mutant Sitters",
    "Ran and Shaw",
    "Raph & Leo, Sibling Rivals",
    "Raph & Mikey, Troublemakers",
    "Splinter & Leo, Father & Son",
    "The Fantastic Four",
    "The Immortal Weapons",
    "The Neutrinos",
    "The Notary Hobbits",
    "The Sackville-Bagginses",
    "Tokka & Rahzar, Terrible Twos",
    "Tom, Bert, and William",
    "Tui and La, Moon and Ocean",
]
